/external/*

# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/
.DS_Store

# User data files (may be created during testing)
.fastembed_cache/
.*
!.gitignore
!.gitattributes
!.github/
# Each website-*/ deploys as a Cloudflare Worker whose static-assets directory
# is ".", so its .assetsignore is what keeps deploy.sh and wrangler.toml from
# being published as site content. The blanket `.*` above had left the MD,
# Verse and World ones untracked, which a fresh clone would have deployed
# without.
!.assetsignore

# Compiled libraries
*.a
*.so
*.dylib
*.dll

# Website dependencies
website/node_modules/

# Xcode / Apple app build artifacts
**/DerivedData/
**/xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
*.ipa
*.dSYM.zip

# Opencode
opencode.json

# Wrangler local state for the landing pages (website-gen, website-md,
# website-verse each deploy as their own static-assets Worker).
website-*/.wrangler/

# website-world/ is assembled, not stored. `scripts/assemble.mjs` copies the
# viewer and the conformance scenes in from crates/ (so they cannot drift from
# the apps the way the old cross-repo sync did), and the curated worlds' shrunk
# GLBs, music and posters in from the assets checkout, where they are LFS
# objects. Only the site's own source is tracked here.
website-world/viewer/world-viewer.js
website-world/worlds/assets/
website-world/worlds/posters/
website-world/worlds/behaviors.json
website-world/worlds/hierarchy_tours.json
website-world/worlds/lights.json
website-world/worlds/materials.json
website-world/worlds/shapes.json
website-world/worlds/soundtrack.json
website-world/worlds/textures.json
website-world/node_modules/
